.\" sgrn_dataset.1 - manual page for sgrn_dataset
.TH SGRN_DATASET 1 "September 2026" "SGRN 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sgrn_dataset \- SGRN Industrial Telemetry Dataset Processor & Data Canonicalizer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sgrn_dataset
\-i \fIDIR\fR \-s \fISCHEMA.scl\fR [\-c \fIDATASET.csv\fR] [\-m \fIMANIFEST.json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sgrn_dataset
is the C++ data canonicalization engine for the SGRN platform. It reads Zstd-compressed JSON Lines (.jsonl.zst) telemetry archives generated by the SGRN Gateway persistence service, reconciles state deltas, applies SCL schema rules (including #UNIT directives and categorical enum mappings), and exports a normalized CSV dataset alongside a structured Machine Learning manifest JSON file.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-i\fR, \fB\-\-input\fR \fIDIR\fR
Path to the input directory containing Zstd historian archives (.jsonl.zst or .jsonl). Required.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-scl\fR \fIFILE.scl\fR
Path to the SCL schema file (.scl) defining PLC data blocks, variable types, and #UNIT physical unit annotations. Required.
.TP
\fB\-c\fR, \fB\-\-csv\fR \fIFILE.csv\fR
Path to the output CSV file where aligned time-series feature rows will be written. Default: \fIdataset.csv\fR.
.TP
\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-manifest\fR \fIFILE.json\fR
Path to the output ML Manifest JSON file containing feature taxonomy, units, categorical enum maps, and empirical statistics. Default: \fImanifest.json\fR.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Display command usage help and exit.

.SH SCHEMA ANNOTATIONS & #UNIT CONVENTIONS
Tag names in SCL schemas must be unit-agnostic. Physical units are annotated directly on variables using the \fB#UNIT("...")\fR directive:

.nf
DATA_BLOCK "Reactor"
{
    VERSION: '0.1'
}
STRUCT
    thermal_power   #UNIT("MW")   : REAL := 3400.0;
    przr_pressure   #UNIT("bar")  : REAL := 155.0;
END_STRUCT
END_DATA_BLOCK
.fi

.SH EXAMPLES
Extract a canonical dataset from telemetry archives using nuclear schema:
.IP
.B sgrn_dataset \-\-input /tmp/sgrn\-state/ \-\-scl ./schema.scl \-\-csv dataset.csv \-\-manifest manifest.json

.SH ARCHITECTURAL ROLE
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSGRN Gateway\fR: Operational live state twin.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBsgrn_dataset\fR: C++ data canonicalizer producing row-aligned datasets.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSGRN Datastore\fR: Persistent cloud substrate storing manifests, model weights, and schemas.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gateway (1),
.BR s7shell (1),
.BR sgrn_datastore (1)
